{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>From the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob.</b> This came to him from the Holy One, blessed be He, who is the Mighty One of Jacob, and from there he merited to be the shepherd of Eben Israel — the chief foundation of Israel, in the sense of הָאֶבֶן הָרֹאשָׁה (Zechariah 4:7). This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 49:24). <b>From the El of your father</b> — this came to you and He will help you, and with the Holy One, blessed be He, was your heart, when you did not heed the words of your mistress, and He will bless you — this too is his language. And Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] said that the mem of מֵאֵל אָבִיךָ extends to וְאֵת שַׁדַּי, and He will bless you.\n\nAnd by way of truth, this blessing resembles the blessing with which he blessed the youths above, for the Mighty One of Jacob is the Elohim of truth, and Scripture never says the Mighty One of Abraham or of Isaac or others, but only the Mighty One of Jacob or the Mighty One of Israel (Isaiah 49:26) — that is, the Mighty One of Israel (Isaiah 1:24). He is Jacob. And behold: מִידֵי אֲבִיר יַעֲקֹב — the greatness and the might; from there, מִידֵי אֲבִיר יַעֲקֹב, רֹעֶה אֶבֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל — she is the chief cornerstone that became the head of the corner (Psalms 118:22), from before YHWH. And it is called אֶבֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל, as the Sages said: Knesset Israel is the chief cornerstone. And the meaning of אֶבֶן is that it is a building that completes everything. And the meaning of רֹעֶה is that the power in the might is exalted by the right hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is written: קַרְנַיִם מִיָּדוֹ לוֹ וְשָׁם חֶבְיוֹן עֻזּוֹ (Habakkuk 3:4), meaning: and there, in His right hand, is the hidden power of might; and חֶבְיוֹן is the exalted force hidden away in the place of His nobility. And this is what is said: וְכַנָּה אֲשֶׁר נָטְעָה יְמִינֶךָ (Psalms 80:16) — מֵאֵל אָבִיךָ, הָאֱלֹהִים הָרֹעֶה אֹתִי מֵעוֹדִי, וְאֵת שַׁדַּי וִיבָרְכֶךָּ. And the meaning of the blessing is: מִידֵי אֲבִיר יַעֲקֹב — from the Chesed that shepherds Eben Israel, and from the Elohim of his father — He will draw forth favor and His help will come; and with Shaddai will be His blessing, and behold, He is blessed in heaven and on earth. And this is the meaning of בִּרְכֹת אָבִיךָ גָּבְרוּ עַל בִּרְכֹת הוֹרַי — for the building is complete in him. Thus have I drawn up this matter from the midrash of Rabbi Nechunya ben HaKanah (see Sefer HaBahir §§193, 148), and the enlightened will understand."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Isaiah 49:26 for the phrase אֲבִיר יִשְׂרָאֵל; I have supplied the verse address accordingly. The citation in the Hebrew parenthetical '(ישעיהו א כד)' gives Isaiah 1:24 for the same phrase, which is textually correct; 49:26 does not contain it, suggesting a possible variant in Ramban's intent or a scribal interpolation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:47:25.994906943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}